started: 2026-09-09
branch: feature/handler-fusion-gate
worktree: ../okay-wt-fusion
spec: specs/handler-fusion.md (80ecea0e), stage 0

why: the operator proposed composing a row's handlers into one handler
  and staging the composite (2026-09-09). The spec assessed it as right
  and already-half-done; what is not known is the SIZE of the win for
  the continuation-aware class, and the spec makes that a gate: no
  generic code until a hand-written fused loop clears 1.3x.

what: a hand-written fused loop for State % S + Writer % W (one
  @tailrec match over Free, product accumulator, immutable), an
  agreement test on generated programs for BOTH nestings, and JMH
  lanes (µs/op + B/op) against State.handle(Writer.run(p)) and
  Writer.run(State.handle(p)), N=1000; then the three-effect row with
  Throws (no abort taken). Results go into the spec either way.

predict: 1.3-1.8x on two effects, more on three; B/op drops by about
  one Bind + one closure per forwarded operation per saved pass. The
  mechanism that would eat it: resume's rotation costs more than the
  rebuild, and one pass rotates as much as three.

MACHINE: both scalascript launchd guards are LOADED again (bench-refresh
  reloaded them). The ram guard kills the heaviest JVM matching
  sbt-launch|org.openjdk.jmh under memory pressure — a JMH fork of
  mine can die with a 143 that is not a failure. Read
  ~/Library/Logs/kill-stale-builders.log before believing a crash.
